From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WinHubWine debug-friendly fork
Date: Thu, 7 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shell32/shlfileop: normalize bare drive root ("C:") to
 "C:\\" in file_entry_init

When SHFileOperationW is called with a destination like "D:" (no
trailing backslash), file_entry_init() previously failed to populate
szDirectory and szFilename because wcsrchr(file_name, '\\') returns
NULL for the bare "X:" form. The two fields were left NULL.

Later, do_copy_move() does:

    wcscpy(target_dir, to->szDirectory);       // NULL -> segfault
    PathAppendW(target_dir, to->szFilename);  // NULL -> segfault

so copying/moving between drive roots via File Explorer (or any
caller that passes bare "X:") crashes with a NULL pointer fault.

This matches the gamenative patch set description:
    "shell32 shlfileop.c: Properly handles drive root paths without
     backslashes, fixing a crash that occurred when copying between
     root directories in File Explorer."

Fix: detect the bare drive root form (single letter, ':', NUL) at
the top of file_entry_init, allocate one extra WCHAR, and write
"X:\\0" into szFullPath so wcsrchr() finds the trailing backslash
and szDirectory / szFilename get populated normally.

Behavior matches real Windows: for SHFileOperation copy/move, a
bare "X:" is treated as the drive root, not as "current directory
on drive X" (which is the GetFullPathName semantics but not the
SHFileOperation semantics).

Pure additive bug fix; no performance impact (one length check +
one extra WCHAR allocation in the rare bare-drive-root case).
---
 dlls/shell32/shlfileop.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/dlls/shell32/shlfileop.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shlfileop.c
@@ -947,8 +947,28 @@
     size_t file_name_len = wcslen(file_name) + 1;
     const WCHAR *ptr;
 
-    file_entry->szFullPath = malloc(file_name_len * sizeof(WCHAR));
-    wcscpy(file_entry->szFullPath, file_name);
+    /* Normalize a bare drive root (e.g., "C:") to "C:\\" so that
+     * wcsrchr() below finds a backslash and szDirectory / szFilename
+     * get populated. Without this, copying/moving to a bare "X:"
+     * destination leaves both fields NULL and do_copy_move() crashes
+     * dereferencing them. Matches real Windows SHFileOperation
+     * semantics where "X:" == "X:\\" for copy/move destinations.
+     */
+    if (file_name_len == 3 && isalpha(file_name[0]) && file_name[1] == ':')
+    {
+        file_entry->szFullPath = malloc(4 * sizeof(WCHAR));
+        file_entry->szFullPath[0] = file_name[0];
+        file_entry->szFullPath[1] = ':';
+        file_entry->szFullPath[2] = '\\';
+        file_entry->szFullPath[3] = '\0';
+        file_name = file_entry->szFullPath;
+        file_name_len = 4;
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        file_entry->szFullPath = malloc(file_name_len * sizeof(WCHAR));
+        wcscpy(file_entry->szFullPath, file_name);
+    }
 
     ptr = wcsrchr(file_name, '\\');
     if (ptr)
